            <ArticleTitle>Clinical predictors of mortality in patients with Ebola virus disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1821-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/cid/civ202</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In an observational cohort study including 89 Ebola patients, predictive factors of death were analyzed. The crude mortality rate was 43.8%. Myalgia (adjusted odds ratio [OR], 4.04; P = .02), hemorrrhage (adjusted OR, 3.5; P = .02), and difficulty breathing (adjusted OR, 5.75; P = .01) were independently associated with death.</AbstractText>
